  era: "c. 1900 BCE \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Why did the cities decline?
  text: From about 1900 BCE the cities declined. Explanations include climate change and weaker monsoons, the drying of the Ghaggar-Hakra river, shifting rivers and floods, and the collapse of trade. The once-popular idea of an Aryan invasion is no longer accepted as the cause.
